<<<
+ only, but it does not follow that there are not often good reasons for departing from orthodoxy. For He only died a week ago no better
===
+ only, but it does not follow that there are not often good reasons for departing from orthodoxy. For ***He only died a week ago*** no better
>>>

<<<
because the intonation of died is entirely different if it, & not a week ago, is qualified by only; & it is fair
===
because the intonation of *died* is entirely different if it, & not *a week ago*, is qualified by *only*; & it is fair
>>>

<<<
placing is much stronger:—Mackenzie only seems to go wrong when he lets in yellow; & yellow seems to be still the standing difficulty of the colour printer. The orthodox place for only is immediately before when, & the antithesis
===
placing is much stronger:—*Mackenzie only seems to go wrong when he lets in yellow; & yellow seems to be still the standing difficulty of the colour printer.* The orthodox place for *only* is immediately before *when*, & the antithesis
>>>

<<<
a quite sound rhetorical instinct, &, if goes had been used instead of seems to go, a sufficient
===
a quite sound rhetorical instinct, &, if *goes* had been used instead of *seems to go*, a sufficient
>>>

